concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-act-2001-sec-5-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5(5) Entities covered by the Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-5-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) A discretionary mutual fund is a fund (however constituted) for making payments on the happening of a specified event (where there is uncertainty as to whether, or when, the event will happen), that is a fund: (a) to which 2 or more persons contribute, and: (i) out of which payments may be made in respect of liabilities, losses, damages or expenses of the contributors; and (ii) that is governed by rules under which any such payment for the benefit of a contributor is subject to a discretion of a person or body; or (b) that is declared to be a discretionary mutual fund, or included in a class of funds that are declared to be discretionary mutual funds, by regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph." ;
    skos:definition "(5) A discretionary mutual fund is a fund (however constituted) for making payments on the happening of a specified event (where there is uncertainty as to whether, or when, the event will happen), that is a fund: (a) to which 2 or more persons contribute, and: (i) out of which payments may be made in respect of liabilities, losses, damages or expenses of the contributors; and (ii) that is governed by rules under which any such payment for the benefit of a contributor is subject to a discretion of a person or body; or (b) that is declared to be a discretionary mutual fund, or included in a class of funds that are declared to be discretionary mutual funds, by regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d763961f9e5a03711880aa3dc7f531990810fa05ad54c83acb74978bf77e6f3d" ;
    values:partOf concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-act-2001-sec-5 ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Entities covered by the Act" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
