tituted for the period referred to in that subsection. (4) Neither subsection (1) nor (2) applies to a corporation if, before the end of the period referred to in that subsection (including any period that is taken to be substituted for that period by any application or applications of subsection (3) in relation to that corporation), the corporation ceases to be a registrable corporation. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to matters in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code). (5) The documents referred to in subsections (1) and (2) are: (a) a statement in writing setting out:" ;
