concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-act-2001-sec-14 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "14 Principal executive officer of financial sector entity (other than a"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-14 ;
    values:originalText "superannuation entity) to notify the entity’s governing body of a failure to provide reporting documents to APRA (1) This section applies if a financial sector entity (other than a superannuation entity) that is required by or under a reporting standard to give a reporting document to APRA before a particular time or within a particular period fails to comply with the requirement. (2) It is the duty of the principal executive officer of the entity, as soon as practicable after that time or the end of that period, as the case may be, to notify the governing body of the entity in writing that the failure has occurred. (3) The principal executive officer of a financial sector entity must not refuse or fail to notify the governing body of the entity as required by subsection (2). Penalty: 50 penalty units.   Provision of documents to APRA  Part 3 Determination of reporting standards and requirement to provide documents  Division 2 Section 15 Financial Sector (Collection of Data) Act 2001 Compilation date: 21/02/2025 (4) An offence for a contravention of subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability. 15  When reporting standards begin to apply to particular financial sector entities (1) The reporting standards apply to a financial sector entity only on and after the day declared by APRA to be the day on which the standards begin to apply to the entity or to the class or kind of financial sector entities in which the entity is included. (2) APRA may, by writing published in the Gazette, make declarations for the purposes of subsection (1)." ;
    skos:definition "superannuation entity) to notify the entity’s governing body of a failure to provide reporting documents to APRA (1) This section applies if a financial sector entity (other than a superannuation entity) that is required by or under a reporting standard to give a reporting document to APRA before a particular time or within a particular period fails to comply with the requirement. (2) It is the duty of the principal executive officer of the entity, as soon as practicable after that time or the end of that period, as the case may be, to notify the governing body of the entity in writing that the failure has occurred. (3) The principal executive officer of a financial sector entity must not refuse or fail to notify the governing body of the entity as required by subsection (2). Penalty: 50 penalty units.   Provision of documents to APRA  Part 3 Determination of reporting standards and requirement to provide documents  Division 2 Section 15 Financial Sector (Collection of Data) Act 2001 Compilation date: 21/02/2025 (4) An offence for a contravention of subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability. 15  When reporting standards begin to apply to particular financial sector entities (1) The reporting standards apply to a financial sector entity only on and after the day declared by APRA to be the day on which the standards begin to apply to the entity or to the class or kind of financial sector entities in which the entity is included. (2) APRA may, by writing published in the Gazette, make declarations for the purposes of subsection (1)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b494cb82f6c7df228620c6dbbba2a6caffdd2916ccb6680cdc6c8d66e8067a1b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-act-2001-sec-14-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-act-2001-sec-14-ss-2 ;
