doc:sec-17-ss-8 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "17(8) APRA may require the variation of a reporting document or the" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(8) A financial sector entity must comply with a direction given to it under subsection (3) or (4) or with such a direction as varied under subsection (6) or (7), as the case requires. Penalty: 50 penalty units." ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer .

concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-act-2001-sec-17-ss-9 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "17(9) APRA may require the variation of a reporting document or the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-17-ss-9 ;
    values:originalText "(9) To avoid doubt, section 4K of the Crimes Act 1914 applies to an obligation imposed by subsection (8). Note: The effect of section 4K of the Crimes Act 1914 is that, if a financial sector entity refuses or fails to comply with a direction before the time, or within the period, specified in the direction, the obligation to comply with the direction continues after that time or that period with daily offences being committed until the direction is complied with." ;
    skos:definition "(9) To avoid doubt, section 4K of the Crimes Act 1914 applies to an obligation imposed by subsection (8). Note: The effect of section 4K of the Crimes Act 1914 is that, if a financial sector entity refuses or fails to comply with a direction before the time, or within the period, specified in the direction, the obligation to comply with the direction continues after that time or that period with daily offences being committed until the direction is complied with."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "54c32079e9cfaa917868adabaacb4c90766dfe444b544e860de7ff035e5342bc" ;
    values:partOf concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-act-2001-sec-17 ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Section 4K of the Crimes Act 1914 applies to an obligation imposed by subsection (8)" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
