concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-act-2001-sec-17d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "17D Giving false or misleading information to auditor"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-17d ;
    values:originalText "Offence—person knows the information is false or misleading etc. (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is: (i) a financial sector entity; or (ii) an employee, officer or trustee of a financial sector entity; and (b) the person gives information, or allows information to be given, to an auditor of the financial sector entity; and (c) the information relates to the affairs of the financial sector entity; and (d) the person knows that the information: (i) is false or misleading in a material particular; or (ii) is missing something that makes the information misleading in a material respect. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 200 penalty units, or both. Offence—person fails to ensure the information is not false or misleading etc. (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is an employee or officer of a financial sector entity; and (b) the person gives information, or allows information to be given, to an auditor of the financial sector entity; and (c) the information relates to the affairs of the financial sector entity; and" ;
    skos:definition "Offence—person knows the information is false or misleading etc. (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is: (i) a financial sector entity; or (ii) an employee, officer or trustee of a financial sector entity; and (b) the person gives information, or allows information to be given, to an auditor of the financial sector entity; and (c) the information relates to the affairs of the financial sector entity; and (d) the person knows that the information: (i) is false or misleading in a material particular; or (ii) is missing something that makes the information misleading in a material respect. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 200 penalty units, or both. Offence—person fails to ensure the information is not false or misleading etc. (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is an employee or officer of a financial sector entity; and (b) the person gives information, or allows information to be given, to an auditor of the financial sector entity; and (c) the information relates to the affairs of the financial sector entity; and"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7ee6657b632cc4e82e71c9c44aa112ced42febde407c3cee1205368d47799384" ;
    cof:pageNumber "35"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-act-2001-sec-17d-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-act-2001-sec-17d-ss-2 ;
